  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1234 AM CDT Fri Sep 4 2026\n\nThe upper-level ridge will pivot toward the High Plains today into\ntomorrow, but hot and humid conditions will still push heat index\nvalues into the 105-110 range across most of the area. An easterly\nwave bringing a renewed surge of moisture will support shower and\nthunderstorm development early enough in the Pine Belt of\nsoutheast Mississippi today that heat should be less of a concern\nthere. Tomorrow looks to have a similar setup, and then the ridge\nand northwest flow will squeeze rain chances closer to the Gulf\nCoast. North of the better rain chances, daily heat index values\ncould even approach or exceed 110 degrees. For the time being,\nwill maintain an \"Elevated\" threat area for dangerous heat stress\non local Hazardous Weather Outlook graphics Sunday into early \nnext week. /NF/",
